6 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7bc16273-b0c3-5d3e-ada8-6f51530d1b3a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291280 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291280 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291280 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "958b3c28-fb33-5d0f-a319-72156a7d2c54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292186 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "91075236-9924-59d0-8be0-f3ed9e73279b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186290940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292488 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f1d95fed-6abb-5898-9ccd-fc77f7d79a43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2689" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the global minimum value of the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}$ on the closed interval $-3\\le x\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a9c0cbdb-b0ad-5562-a0b0-37a865ff6d3d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292683 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)={x}^{4}-8{x}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-16x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}-16x & =0 \\\\ 4x({x}^{2}-4) & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-2)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,0,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-3,1]$, the critical points are $x=-2,0,$ and the endpoints $x=-3,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =(-3)^{4}-8(-3)^{2}=9 \\\\ f(-2) & =(-2)^{4}-8(-2)^{2}=-16 \\\\ f(0) & =(0)^{4}-8(0)^{2}=0 \\\\ f(1) & =(1)^{4}-8(1)^{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-3)=9,$ so the global maximum is $9.$\n\n- The least value is $f(-2)=-16,$ so the global minimum is $-16.$\n\n![](images/e5/e57ff9bc04fb9d9db592dda6aac9c364fd5f2e6fcd52968627b1e0271919f5bb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1071 "Find  the global minimum value of the function $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8383b31-3ef6-56e1-8528-1bcdbd1b3b84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292730 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{2}(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =3(-1)^{4}-8(-1)^{3}+3=14 \\\\ f(0) & =3(0)^{4}-8(0)^{3}+3=3 \\\\ f(1) & =3(1)^{4}-8(1)^{3}+3=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(-1)=14,$ so the global maximum is $14.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=-2,$ so the global minimum is $-2.$\n\n![](images/9a/9ac7f0c0e28532c897e1c89a35e9c027f614fee40b4b94362a6c5cb012c8a7f6.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452712 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452713 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186452714 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1069 "q-79341" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1071 "For the function $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ on the closed interval $-1\\le x\\le 1,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The global maximum value is $\\frac{9}{e}$\n- **II.** The global maximum value is $4$\n- **III.** The global minimum value is $e$" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "199c3a81-6b01-5801-addf-6e540efda73d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348211 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =2(x-2){e}^{x}+(x-2)^{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x}[2+x-2] \\\\  & =x(x-2){e}^{x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nx(x-2){e}^{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\\,2.\n$$\n\nSince $x=2$ does not belong to the interval $[-1,1]$, the critical points are $x=0$ and the endpoints $x=-1,1$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1-2)^{2}{e}^{-1}=\\frac{9}{e}≈3.31 \\\\ f(0) & =(0-2)^{2}{e}^{0}=4 \\\\ f(1) & =(1-2)^{2}{e}^{1}=e≈2.72\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(0)=4,$ so the global maximum is $4.$\n\n- The least value is $f(1)=e,$ so the global minimum is $e.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"\n\n![](images/ad/adeb7eb92f270a216f30cd0466e91d0363c5a50b17053316e6e9f44d0dfaaf23.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186446051 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446051 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446051 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14e95874-53a9-59eb-a59d-1506787a86d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446052 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446052 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446052 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28e244bd-f5d9-59e7-bae1-37bf7dad0604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446057 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446057 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446057 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83b3d4b4-9193-548b-92d2-89f90a26ba3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446063 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446063 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446063 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf0fca65-f9f6-5b4c-986e-f335607b1999" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446065 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446065 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446065 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cca7c6b4-7bda-5ecf-9402-b6c9fb9f1393" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186446065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446073 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eafc929c-fdf4-5237-8e6e-4e3e669ade96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the global maximum value of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ on the closed interval $0\\le x\\le 2\\pi .$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6d6fccce-a1a6-5495-8484-833c6aab421e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186446079 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi n,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer. We discard all solutions except $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ and $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi =\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ since they are the only values that belong to the given interval.\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ and the endpoints $x=0,\\,2\\pi $ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=-1 \\\\ f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ f(2\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2},$ so the global maximum is $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=-\\sqrt{2},$ so the global minimum is $-\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n![](images/76/7645cecb4fef2af4f2e2061752957981414d63700de016ca4a535c8df219597e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186450156 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450156 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450156 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69c09760-2d64-5dc1-bd95-dbf93b49b75e" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450157 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aeb90533-2e1f-508d-a49f-33cb04df8165" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450158 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450158 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186450158 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1840414b-3944-5796-ad10-fefa